  "placementWhy": "Scale bar (45 m) and north (magnetic 2006, declination 0 deg 02' E: up), shifted onto Entrada Tixik K'una, the map's datum. This edition gives no coordinate; the later edition (July 2008, 4978.8 m, -27.6 m; photo _data/cartes/Sistema Tixik K'una.jpg) prints 'WGS84 Datum 16Q 0462536 UTM 2248847' at the entrance, blurry: the easting's third digit reads as 3 as easily as 2, but 463536 would put the entrance 300 m from the beach east of highway 307, against the map's own note (1.2 km from the sea) and its trail SE to the highway; 462536 lands 13 m from the database's Templo Dry Cave (Gerrard). Check: the database's Templo (Gerrard: a dry cenote behind a Maya temple) falls 39 m from Entradas Las Ruinas (bearing 294 vs 300 deg, 206 vs 186 m). The canopy hides everything on the satellite; no other placed map overlaps. A field GPS of either entrance would settle it.",
  "sistemaWhy": "Tixik K'una (-KPZgfySFFmEXg_2MfP8), no position or caves in the database. Its two entrances seem to be the database's Templo and Templo Dry Cave (Gerrard), filed under sistema Templo (-KPZgfyNcD9jUSzJuPQu, 1680 m, 21 m): Sifon Templo, at this map's NW end, is the sump into Templo's flooded cave. The user may want to link the two sistemas.",
  "notWalls": "Thin lines: floor detail (stipple, slopes, boulders, drip-line ticks), cross-section leaders (erased); the double-dashed surface trails Brecha a Las Ruinas and Brecha a Carretera Federal 307 (erased). Grey fills: medium grey = water, light grey = rock halo outside the walls and pillars."
